# P2 implementation report

P2 adds the native live admission guard at both points required to prevent unadmitted paid work: after each complete request is built but before runtime persistence, and inside the existing ledger transition before reservation construction and append.

The shared reader preserves the legacy path by rediscovering enrollment and returning immediately when absent. For enrolled campaigns it authenticates the policy envelope, original manifest/launch/config/root/owner, selected round configuration/start, stored deadlines, prior settled resource history, checkpoint/archive projection, committed evaluated records and their accepted critic, request/journal identities, and the exact verified ledger prefix. It permits only the exact current request/call recovery tail, rejects later/conflicting/orphan selected state, rejects new work in a settled current round, and applies the P1 boundary decision to the immutable prefix before the current round.

`production_runtime.py` contains one factory helper and exactly three guarded request returns. `production_provider.py` retains the old content lookup, budget predicate, slot construction, and `lease_started` order for unenrolled ledgers. Enrolled ledgers additionally require the unique persisted call/request and repeat the shared guard before reservation creation; no second transition was added.

Independent review of freeze 01 found five gaps. Fix round 1 now binds the incoming ledger attempt identity, requires accepted current predecessors before any next call or tail, applies native prior-stop precedence, propagates failed foreign-config authentication, and performs a fresh real-time deadline check after immutable authentication and the boundary decision. The exact reviewed freeze and original diff remain in `review-freeze-01/`; the narrow correction is `fix-round-1.diff`.

The corrected source is frozen at the hashes in `source-freeze.md`. The updated three-file unified diff is `actual-task.diff`. Ruff, in-memory compile, focused source/AST protection checks, and the earlier 662-archive-file plus 56-evaluator-file byte preservation check passed. Dynamic tests and operational readers were prohibited and were not run. Independent fix review remains the next gate before any later increment changes these files.
